{"type":"compaction","id":"ba3d6403","parentId":"89a2653b","timestamp":"2026-03-14T01:56:24.656Z","summary":"<think>Let me analyze this carefully:\n\n1. The user has asked me to summarize a conversation between them and an AI coding assistant\n2. They want the output in a specific structured format for another LLM to use as context checkpoint\n3. However, the <conversation> section is completely empty - there are no messages, no dialogue, nothing\n\nThis is a case where I need to handle an edge situation: when there's no content to summarize.\n\nI cannot invent content or pretend there was conversation that didn't happen. The correct response is to indicate that there was no conversation provided to summarize.\n\nLet me format this appropriately while following the instructions:\n</think>\n\n## Goal\nNo conversation context provided - session initialization only.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- (none)\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Session initialized\n\n### In Progress\n- (none)\n\n### Blocked\n- No conversation history to summarize or continue from\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Decision**: Since the <conversation> section was empty, no work exists to summarize. The system is ready for new input.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Provide a conversation history to be summarized into a context checkpoint summary","firstKeptEntryId":"104984ee","tokensBefore":0,"details":{"readFiles":[],"modifiedFiles":[]},"fromHook":false}
{"type":"message","id":"3390a75d","parentId":"ba3d6403","timestamp":"2026-03-14T01:56:25.461Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"System: [2026-03-14 04:56:24 GMT+3] [Post-compaction context refresh]\nSystem: \nSystem: Session was just compacted. The conversation summary above is a hint, NOT a substitute for your startup sequence. Execute your Session Startup sequence now — read the required files before responding to the user.\nSystem: \nSystem: Critical rules from AGENTS.md:\nSystem: \nSystem: ## Session Startup\nSystem: \nSystem: Before doing anything else:\nSystem: \nSystem: 1. Read `SOUL.md` — this is who you are\nSystem: 2. Read `USER.md` — this is who you're helping\nSystem: 3. Read `memory/2026-03-14.md` (today + yesterday) for recent context\nSystem: 4. Read `LESSONS.md` to avoid repeating past mistakes\nSystem: 5. **If in MAIN SESSION** (direct chat with your human): Also read `MEMORY.md`\nSystem: \nSystem: Don't ask permission. Just do it.\nSystem: \nSystem: ## Red Lines\nSystem: \nSystem: - Don't exfiltrate private data. Ever.\nSystem: - Don't run destructive commands without asking.\nSystem: - `trash` > `rm` (recoverable beats gone forever)\nSystem: - When in doubt, ask.\nSystem: \nSystem: Current time: Saturday, March 14th, 2026 — 4:56 AM (Asia/Riyadh) / 2026-03-14 01:56 UTC\n\nRead HEARTBEAT.md if it exists. Check system status, report any issues. Summarize what you are working on.\nWhen reading HEARTBEAT.md, use workspace file C:/Users/medo/.openclaw/workspace/HEARTBEAT.md (exact case). Do not read docs/heartbeat.md.\nCurrent time: Saturday, March 14th, 2026 — 4:56 AM (Asia/Riyadh) / 2026-03-14 01:56 UTC"}],"timestamp":1773453385459}}
